<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  PhoneZero TeXML Bin content.

  TeXML Bins are STATIC documents hosted by Telnyx. Telnyx fetches this XML
  as-is when the outbound restaurant call is answered. There is no per-call
  templating at runtime.

  Placeholders are substituted ONCE at setup time (the Bot or a human pastes
  the filled document into the TeXML Bin editor). After that the bin never
  changes between calls.

  Setup-time placeholder:
    {PHONEZERO_XAI_SIP_NUMBER}
      The xAI Voice Agent SIP-connected number (user/digits only, no sip:
      prefix). Example fixture after substitution: +15555550101

  Verified against:
    https://developers.telnyx.com/docs/voice/programmable-voice/texml-verbs/dial
    https://developers.telnyx.com/docs/voice/programmable-voice/texml-setup
    https://developers.telnyx.com/docs/voice/programmable-voice/texml-bin-quickstart
    https://developers.telnyx.com/docs/voice/programmable-voice/texml-answering-machine
    https://developers.telnyx.com/docs/voice/texml/rest-api/transcripts
-->
<Response>
  <!--
    <Dial> bridges the already-answered restaurant leg to the xAI voice agent.

    record="record-from-answer-dual"
      Official Dial @record values (default do-not-record):
        do-not-record | record-from-answer | record-from-ringing |
        record-from-answer-dual | record-from-ringing-dual
      record-from-answer-dual starts a dual-channel recording when the SIP
      destination answers. Verified:
      https://developers.telnyx.com/docs/voice/programmable-voice/texml-verbs/dial

    recordingChannels="dual"
      Official values: single | dual (default single). Stereo: one party per
      channel. Set explicitly so dual is not lost if record is later changed
      to record-from-answer. Same Dial page as above.

    timeout="30"
      Seconds to wait for the SIP destination (xAI) to answer. Range 5–120,
      default 30. Same Dial page.

    timeLimit="600"
      Max bridged-call duration in seconds. Range 60–14400, default 14400.
      600s (10 min) is a sensible restaurant-booking cap. Same Dial page.

    answerOnBridge is omitted: this Dial runs after Telnyx has already
    answered the REST-originated restaurant call (TeXML is fetched on
    answer). answerOnBridge only preserves ringing on an unanswered inbound
    leg. Same Dial page.

    recordingStatusCallback is omitted: PhoneZero is zero-server; the Bot
    polls recordings via TeXML REST instead of receiving webhooks.

    AMD is NOT set on this <Sip>. Dial <Number>/<Sip> do support
    machineDetection (Enable | DetectMessageEnd | Disable) — that classifies
    the DESTINATION of this Dial, which is the xAI agent, not the restaurant.
    Restaurant AMD belongs on the REST initiate-call request
    (MachineDetection). See scripts/place-call.sh and:
    https://developers.telnyx.com/docs/voice/programmable-voice/texml-verbs/dial
    https://developers.telnyx.com/docs/voice/programmable-voice/texml-answering-machine

    Transcription: the Dial verb has no transcription attributes. Telnyx
    documents TeXML transcription only for <Record transcription="true">
    and the <Transcription> verb — not for Dial-verb recordings. See
    scripts/get-outcome.sh and:
    https://developers.telnyx.com/docs/voice/texml/rest-api/transcripts
    https://developers.telnyx.com/docs/voice/programmable-voice/texml-verbs/record
  -->
  <Dial
    record="record-from-answer-dual"
    recordingChannels="dual"
    timeout="30"
    timeLimit="600">
    <!--
      <Sip> noun: SIP URI to dial. Official examples use sip:user@host:
      https://developers.telnyx.com/docs/voice/programmable-voice/texml-verbs/dial
      TeXML Bin quickstart also shows user@host without the sip: scheme:
      https://developers.telnyx.com/docs/voice/programmable-voice/texml-bin-quickstart
      We use the sip: form from the Dial verb page.

      ;transport=tls is a SIP URI parameter (RFC 3261), not a TeXML
      attribute. The Dial <Sip> attribute list does not document a
      transport= flag. xAI's SIP endpoint is specified as TLS by PhoneZero.

      {PHONEZERO_XAI_SIP_NUMBER} is replaced once at setup. The published
      bin must contain a real number, not this token.
    -->
    <Sip>sip:{PHONEZERO_XAI_SIP_NUMBER}@sip.voice.x.ai;transport=tls</Sip>
  </Dial>
</Response>
